Now implement ScheduleService. Key logic:

```java
@Service
public class ScheduleService {
    private final ScheduleRepository repository;
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;

    public StoredResponse submit(SubmitRequest req) {
        // validate
        // fingerprint
        // idempotency check
        // process in transaction
    }
}
```

Structure: 
- `submit` (non-transactional wrapper): validates input, computes fingerprint, checks existing request → replay or 409. Otherwise calls `processSubmit` (@Transactional, self-invocation problem!). Self-invocation of @Transactional doesn't work. Options: make submit itself @Transactional and handle replay inside; but the DuplicateKeyException catch needs to be outside the tx. Approach: two beans or use TransactionTemplate. I'll use TransactionTemplate injected via PlatformTransactionManager — clean and avoids self-invocation issues.

Plan for submit:
```java
public StoredResponse submit(SubmitRequest req) {
    validate(req);
    WindowRow window = repository.findWindow(req.windowCode()).orElseThrow(404);
    // validate satellite/station codes match window
    String fingerprint = fingerprint(req);
    Optional<RequestRow> existing = repository.findRequest(req.requestId());
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        RequestRow row = existing.get();
        if (!row.fingerprint().equals(fingerprint)) throw conflict IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT;
        return new StoredResponse(row.httpStatus(), row.responseBody());
    }
    try {
        return txTemplate.execute(status -> doSubmit(req, window, fingerprint));
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        // 并发：同 requestId 已由他事务提交，或同站同窗已被抢占
        Optional<RequestRow> won = repository.findRequest(req.requestId());
        if (won.isPresent() && won.get().fingerprint().equals(fingerprint)) {
            return new StoredResponse(won.get().httpStatus(), won.get().responseBody());
        }
        throw ApiException.conflict("CONCURRENT_CONFLICT", "并发申请冲突：同一地面站同一窗口仅允许一个成功");
    }
}
```

Wait — DuplicateKeyException inside txTemplate.execute: the transaction will be rolled back by the template when the exception propagates. Good.

But there's a subtlety: DuplicateKeyException may be thrown at commit time rather than at insert time? With H2, constraint checked at insert. OK.

doSubmit:
```java
private StoredResponse doSubmit(req, window, fingerprint) {
    boolean frozen = repository.existsPublication(window.day());
    List<EntryRow> conflicts = repository.findConflictingEntries(window.stationId(), window.startUtc(), window.endUtc());
    List<PreemptedInfo> preempted = new ArrayList<>();
    if (!conflicts.isEmpty()) {
        boolean canPreempt = !frozen && conflicts.stream().allMatch(c -> c.priority() < req.priority());
        if (!canPreempt) {
            // 构造冲突错误响应并存储
            String code = frozen ? "DAY_FROZEN" : "WINDOW_CONFLICT";
            String msg = frozen ? "该日编排已发布冻结，抢占/冲突申请被拒绝" : "窗口冲突：同优先级先到者保留或对方优先级更高";
            ErrorBody body = new ErrorBody(code, msg, conflictInfos);
            return store(req, window, fingerprint, 409, json(body));
        }
        for (EntryRow c : conflicts) {
            repository.markPreempted(c.id(), req.requestId());
            List<String> candidates = repository.findReplanCandidates(c.satelliteId(), c.stationId(), c.endUtc(), c.windowId());
            repository.insertSuggestion(c.id(), c.satelliteId(), c.stationId(), String.join(",", candidates));
            preempted.add(new PreemptedInfo(c.id(), c.requestId(), c.windowCode(), candidates));
        }
    }
    long entryId = repository.insertEntry(...);
    SubmitAccepted accepted = new SubmitAccepted(req.requestId(), preempted.isEmpty() ? "SCHEDULED" : "PREEMPTED_OTHERS", entryId, preempted);
    return store(req, window, fingerprint, 200, json(accepted));
}
```

Wait — frozen day with conflicts: "发布后的抢占、撤销申请一律拒绝" — any conflicting request on frozen day rejected (regardless of priority). Non-conflicting on frozen day → allowed as draft (emergency insert). My code: canPreempt = !frozen && allMatch → if frozen and conflicts exist → reject with DAY_FROZEN. Good.

Hmm, but what about frozen day, conflict with lower-priority entry — reject with DAY_FROZEN. OK.

Also should the 409 conflict response be stored as the idempotent result? Yes — "同键同参返回首次结果". Both success and rejection are stored.

ErrorBody is in common.GlobalExceptionHandler — referencing it from service is a bit awkward but fine; or define details map. I'll build a small Map or reuse ErrorBody record. Reuse `GlobalExceptionHandler.ErrorBody`.

json serialization: inject ObjectMapper (Spring's configured one). `objectMapper.writeValueAsString(...)`, wrap JsonProcessingException in IllegalStateException.

publish:
```java
public PublishResult publish(LocalDate day) {
    return txTemplate.execute(s -> {
        Optional<Integer> max = repository.maxVersion(day);
        List<EntryRow> unpublished = repository.findUnpublishedEntries(day);
        if (max.isPresent() && unpublished.isEmpty()) {
            return new PublishResult(day.toString(), max.get(), 0, true);
        }
        int version = max.orElse(0) + 1;
        repository.assignVersion(day, version);
        repository.insertPublication(day, version, unpublished.size());
        return new PublishResult(day.toString(), version, unpublished.size(), false);
    });
}
```

Hmm — first publish with zero entries: creates version 1 with 0 entries. Fine.

cancel:
```java
public EntryView cancel(long entryId) {
    return txTemplate.execute(s -> {
        EntryRow e = repository.findEntry(entryId).orElseThrow(404);
        if (e.status().equals("CANCELLED")) return toView(e); // 幂等
        if (repository.existsPublication(e.day())) throw conflict("DAY_FROZEN", "该日已发布冻结，撤销申请被拒绝");
        if (!e.status().equals("SCHEDULED")) throw conflict("INVALID_STATE", "仅已编排条目可撤销");
        repository.markCancelled(entryId);
        return toView(repository.findEntry(entryId).get());
    });
}
```

listEntries/listPublications/snapshot: map rows to views. snapshot: if version > maxVersion → 404? If no publication at all → 404 VERSION_NOT_FOUND. I'll check version exists: if version < 1 or > max → 404.

